.TH "CPS-DEVELOP" 1 "" "CPS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\&cps\-develop \- \&Run a shell or command with a recipe's verified toolchain and sources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.HP 4
.B \&cps develop [OPTIONS] <RECIPE> [\-\- <COMMAND>...]
.SH ARGUMENTS
.PP
.B \&<RECIPE>
.TP
.B \&[COMMAND]...
\&Run this command instead of starting an interactive shell
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \&\-\-repo <REPO>
\&Local repository of the toolchain publisher
.TP
.B \&\-\-trust\-root <TRUST_ROOT>
\&Trust root file that matches the recipe's key\-sha256 pin and names the publisher
.TP
.B \&\-\-toolchain\-config <TOOLCHAIN_CONFIG>
\&Worker\-local repository and trust key locations for the pinned publishers [default: $CPS_TOOLCHAIN_CONFIG unless \-\-repo is given]
.TP
.B \&\-\-sources <SOURCES>
\&Directory of the recipe's source inputs at their recipe paths
.TP
.B \&\-\-source\-cache <SOURCE_CACHE>
\&Source cache filled by cps source fetch or cps source import [default: $CPS_SOURCE_CACHE unless \-\-sources is given]
.TP
.B \&\-\-worker\-config <WORKER_CONFIG>
\&Build worker limits: time, scratch space, file, output, and log sizes, and jobs [default: $CPS_WORKER_CONFIG]
.TP
.B \&\-\-option <NAME=VALUE>
\&Override a build option declared in the recipe
.TP
.B \&\-\-workspace <WORKSPACE>
\&Host directory to mount read\-write at /build/workspace
.TP
.B \&\-h, \-\-help
\&Print help
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cps (1)
